            <ArticleTitle>Reversal of ventricular dilatation in aortic regurgitation after valve replacement and cardiac support implant surgery using the CorCap cardiac support device.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>315-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effects of combined aortic valve replacement, coronary bypass surgery, and passive containment surgery in a patient with long-standing aortic regurgitation and marked ventricular dilatation are described. After surgery there was a rapid decrease in left ventricular size and maintained ventricular function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
